WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.340 --> 00:00:05.740
Like any other area in the United States,
the state of Florida has a healthy share of

00:00:05.740 --> 00:00:08.070
urban legends and local myths.

00:00:08.070 --> 00:00:13.690
Take for example the legendary Swamp Ape,
the region’s bigfoot equivalent, a hulking

00:00:13.690 --> 00:00:18.440
creature said to run amok in the state’s
many swamps and aquatic areas, identified

00:00:18.440 --> 00:00:23.230
by its strong, repugnant odor and deep, guttural
throat-calls.

00:00:23.230 --> 00:00:28.230
Or the ghosts of the St. Augustine lighthouse,
a grizzly tale revolving around two young

00:00:28.230 --> 00:00:33.191
girls who drowned in the nearby sea while
their mother was working the lighthouse, too

00:00:33.191 --> 00:00:37.730
distracted to hear the cries of her children
as they were swallowed by the current and

00:00:37.730 --> 00:00:39.370
returned to the brine.

00:00:39.370 --> 00:00:44.590
It’s rumored that on some nights, the twins'
laughter and cries are heard from the top

00:00:44.590 --> 00:00:45.940
of the lighthouse.

00:00:45.940 --> 00:00:46.940
Not scary enough?

00:00:46.940 --> 00:00:48.650
What about the devil’s chair?

00:00:48.650 --> 00:00:54.360
A seemingly ordinary bench located in the
town of Cassadaga that was supposedly built

00:00:54.360 --> 00:00:56.380
by the devil himself.

00:00:56.380 --> 00:01:02.800
Every night, at midnight, the man in red returns
to his bench, and if you sit beside him, he’ll

00:01:02.800 --> 00:01:08.469
whisper wicked, horrible things into your
ear, leaving you forever scarred and haunted

00:01:08.469 --> 00:01:10.399
by the experience.

00:01:10.399 --> 00:01:15.259
Just don’t leave a drink behind when you
run off the bench in terror though, another

00:01:15.259 --> 00:01:19.649
legend says that any unopened bottles left
on the bench will mysteriously be opened and

00:01:19.649 --> 00:01:21.259
drained by the morning.

00:01:21.259 --> 00:01:25.819
Torturing damned souls for eternity makes
you a thirsty guy, we guess.

00:01:25.819 --> 00:01:31.779
But to a seasoned viewer of SCP Explained,
urban legends and local oddities might seem

00:01:31.779 --> 00:01:38.299
a bit mundane in comparison to the strange,
inexplicable anomalies that the SCP Foundation

00:01:38.299 --> 00:01:40.959
regularly researches and contains.

00:01:40.959 --> 00:01:46.489
After all, the truth is almost always stranger
than fiction, and if an actual anomaly gets

00:01:46.489 --> 00:01:51.749
picked up as an urban legend, the SCP Foundation
is going to do everything in their power to

00:01:51.749 --> 00:01:58.490
shut it down, cover it up, and make the story
a little more digestible for the general public.

00:01:58.490 --> 00:02:03.880
That means relying on the same, tired tropes
and cliches we’ve all heard before.

00:02:03.880 --> 00:02:09.830
Cursed dolls, bigfoot-like creatures, ghost
hitchhikers, we all know them, and as fun

00:02:09.830 --> 00:02:15.239
as they are, the most popular stories aren’t
always the most unique or interesting.

00:02:15.239 --> 00:02:19.840
And if you peer deeper underneath the surface,
you can always find kernels of truth in the

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:21.970
most commonplace of legends.

00:02:21.970 --> 00:02:28.050
For example, what’s commonly referred to
as bigfoot, or sasquatch, is actually SCP-1000,

00:02:28.050 --> 00:02:34.000
a super-intelligent, prehistoric race of ape
creatures known as the Children of the Night,

00:02:34.000 --> 00:02:39.250
who were slaughtered by early humans and forced
to hide from the world in order to preserve

00:02:39.250 --> 00:02:40.519
their species.

00:02:40.519 --> 00:02:42.530
A cursed object or location?

00:02:42.530 --> 00:02:47.450
The Foundation deals with those all of the
time, and stories of ghosts are as commonplace

00:02:47.450 --> 00:02:51.030
in the anomalous world as they are in the
ordinary one.

00:02:51.030 --> 00:02:57.519
But what about an anomaly that utilizes urban
legends to further its own nefarious goals?

00:02:57.519 --> 00:03:01.150
One that’s lifeblood is localized to a single
area?

00:03:01.150 --> 00:03:08.200
Today on SCP Explained, we’re going to be
talking about SCP-3640, an anomaly that capitalizes

00:03:08.200 --> 00:03:12.189
on the interest and intrigue those urban legends
generate.

00:03:12.189 --> 00:03:14.790
Specifically those in the state of Florida.

00:03:14.790 --> 00:03:20.200
We already talked about the variety of weird
and creepy stories the state calls its own,

00:03:20.200 --> 00:03:22.659
but what else is Florida known for?

00:03:22.659 --> 00:03:23.659
Tourism?

00:03:23.659 --> 00:03:24.730
Retirement communities?

00:03:24.730 --> 00:03:26.409
Beautiful, summer weather?

00:03:26.409 --> 00:03:30.110
Slightly crazy individuals making news headlines
for ridiculous reasons?

00:03:30.110 --> 00:03:31.920
How about Disney?

00:03:31.920 --> 00:03:37.209
That’s right, the state of Florida is known
for Walt Disney World, the granddaddy of all

00:03:37.209 --> 00:03:42.299
theme parks that brings in millions of tourist
dollars annually, and the hub for some of

00:03:42.299 --> 00:03:45.870
the most iconic characters and stories in
the world.

00:03:45.870 --> 00:03:49.780
If you’ve ever been to Disney World, then
you know about the costumed characters that

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:51.129
roam the park.

00:03:51.129 --> 00:03:56.469
Silent, mascot costume renditions of your
favorite TV and movie characters, posing for

00:03:56.469 --> 00:03:59.170
pictures and having fun with children.

00:03:59.170 --> 00:04:01.519
The park is practically infested with them.

00:04:01.519 --> 00:04:03.379
They seem inescapable!

00:04:03.379 --> 00:04:08.819
It’s pretty understandable that some people
are unsettled by mascots, they can sometimes

00:04:08.819 --> 00:04:10.530
be downright creepy.

00:04:10.530 --> 00:04:17.209
With those unmoving expressions, giant heads,
unnatural movements, and the faces of familiar

00:04:17.209 --> 00:04:22.820
fictional characters, in the right context,
a mascot can be just as scary as any horror

00:04:22.820 --> 00:04:25.680
movie monster or urban legend could ever be.

00:04:25.680 --> 00:04:27.750
Here’s a situation for you.

00:04:27.750 --> 00:04:32.740
You just landed at a Florida airport, you’re
ready to go to Disney World and enjoy a vacation

00:04:32.740 --> 00:04:37.760
after you’ve been worked to exhaustion as
a junior researcher at the SCP Foundation.

00:04:37.760 --> 00:04:41.729
You want to get familiar with the state, but
you’re trying to cut down on your phone

00:04:41.729 --> 00:04:42.729
usage.

00:04:42.729 --> 00:04:47.000
After all, you’re on vacation, why not do
things the old fashioned way and unplug from

00:04:47.000 --> 00:04:48.130
the electronics?

00:04:48.130 --> 00:04:50.990
You spot a brochure rack in the distance,
perfect!

00:04:50.990 --> 00:04:54.669
A paper hub for everything tourist-y in the
area.

00:04:54.669 --> 00:05:00.069
Among the hundreds of jet skiing courses,
beach information, and mini golf pamphlets,

00:05:00.069 --> 00:05:03.400
one brochure in particular stands out to you.

00:05:03.400 --> 00:05:07.699
Maybe it’s your background in the anomalous,
but you just can’t help yourself from picking

00:05:07.699 --> 00:05:11.190
up a booklet on Florida’s urban legends.

00:05:11.190 --> 00:05:15.130
Knowing what’s behind the curtain, working
for the SCP Foundation, really makes these

00:05:15.130 --> 00:05:17.039
types of things more amusing.

00:05:17.039 --> 00:05:21.169
You’ve seen how the sausage was made, and
it’s a lot more terrifying than anything

00:05:21.169 --> 00:05:22.690
known to the general public.

00:05:22.690 --> 00:05:27.150
Heck, you know for a fact that the organization
you work for has more likely than not covered

00:05:27.150 --> 00:05:31.250
up most of the actual incidents that inspired
these local legends.

00:05:31.250 --> 00:05:37.110
Nonetheless, you pick up the brochure, interested
in the self-guided tour of Florida’s paranormal

00:05:37.110 --> 00:05:41.710
hotspots, and you’re impressed to find that
this booklet has it all.

00:05:41.710 --> 00:05:45.699
Everything from Skunk Apes to a cursed doll,
it’s all in here.

00:05:45.699 --> 00:05:48.729
You chuckle, and tuck the pamphlet underneath
your arm.

00:05:48.729 --> 00:05:53.470
But little do you know, you’re about to
experience something more horrifying than

00:05:53.470 --> 00:05:55.730
any urban legend could ever be.

00:05:55.730 --> 00:06:00.860
You see, if you paid attention to your Foundation
briefings before you left the state for Florida,

00:06:00.860 --> 00:06:05.210
you would know that any Foundation personnel
who encounter tourist brochure pamphlets advertising

00:06:05.210 --> 00:06:10.030
self-guided paranormal tours in Florida are
to bring said pamphlets to the Foundation’s

00:06:10.030 --> 00:06:11.690
attention immediately.

00:06:11.690 --> 00:06:17.410
Mobile Task Force Lambda-12, nicknamed “Pest
Control”, is primed on-demand for incidents

00:06:17.410 --> 00:06:19.550
related to these brochurces.

00:06:19.550 --> 00:06:20.550
Why?

00:06:20.550 --> 00:06:26.960
Because they’re a part of a phenomenon categorized
by the SCP Foundation as SCP-3640.

00:06:26.960 --> 00:06:31.330
But what is SCP-3640?

00:06:31.330 --> 00:06:36.099
Why is something as innocuous and fun as a
paranormal travel brochure an object of high

00:06:36.099 --> 00:06:38.129
interest for the SCP Foundation?

00:06:38.129 --> 00:06:42.900
Well, you, someone who should have maybe listened
to the regional briefing conferences back

00:06:42.900 --> 00:06:48.610
at Site-19 before you left on your vacation,
are about to find out.

00:06:48.610 --> 00:06:53.110
After pursuing your booklet and ruminating
over the numerous locations at your disposal,

00:06:53.110 --> 00:06:57.099
you decide to visit one after you get settled
into your hotel.

00:06:57.099 --> 00:07:01.530
After all, you’re about to experience a
week of family-friend fun at the House of

00:07:01.530 --> 00:07:05.970
Mouse, why not partake in a little horror
just to get the blood pumping?

00:07:05.970 --> 00:07:10.419
A bit of living life on the edge before the
scariest thing you have to deal with is a

00:07:10.419 --> 00:07:15.439
$10 bottle of water and a three hour waiting
line to ride that giant golf ball.

00:07:15.439 --> 00:07:20.199
You drive all the way out to the location
the pamphlet specified, a bridge by the name

00:07:20.199 --> 00:07:25.189
of Sunshine Skyway, located right outside
of Tampa Bay.

00:07:25.189 --> 00:07:29.220
Visiting the bridge at night might also get
you a visit from a mysterious and beautiful

00:07:29.220 --> 00:07:35.139
hitchhiker woman, who stands on the side of
the bridge and attempts to flag down cars.

00:07:35.139 --> 00:07:39.010
If you happen to take her in, she’ll begin
to weep, growing progressively louder and

00:07:39.010 --> 00:07:43.350
louder in her screaming and crying until you
reach the other side of the bridge.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:47.750
And when the driver turns back to ask her
what’s wrong, the woman will have vanished

00:07:47.750 --> 00:07:49.289
without a trace.

00:07:49.289 --> 00:07:50.919
Sounds like a fun time, right?

00:07:50.919 --> 00:07:51.949
Maybe you can find her.

00:07:51.949 --> 00:07:56.729
Heck, maybe she’s single and interested
in an enthusiastic and kind junior researcher

00:07:56.729 --> 00:07:58.750
of the SCP Foundation?

00:07:58.750 --> 00:08:02.861
You would never contain her, you’d promise,
having to raise your voice over the sounds

00:08:02.861 --> 00:08:05.740
of her weeping and crying in the backseat
of your car.

00:08:05.740 --> 00:08:07.599
Or, maybe not.

00:08:07.599 --> 00:08:13.060
This vacation time outside of the lab is making
you think some strange, strange stuff.

00:08:13.060 --> 00:08:18.040
Whatever the case is, you want to see a ghost
girl, so you make your way over to the Sunshine

00:08:18.040 --> 00:08:22.039
Skyway at 11 at night, just like the pamphlet
specified.

00:08:22.039 --> 00:08:26.349
The bridge is strangely empty, especially
for what’s usually a crowded stretch of

00:08:26.349 --> 00:08:27.349
the road.

00:08:27.349 --> 00:08:30.939
In fact, now that you realize it, there’s
no one else here.

00:08:30.939 --> 00:08:36.040
Just you, your car, the black night sky, and
the sound of your humming engine.

00:08:36.040 --> 00:08:41.250
Well, up the road you go, looking for this
supposed ghost hitchhiker.

00:08:41.250 --> 00:08:45.640
The Skyway is quite the drive, and the longer
you ride, the less safe you feel.

00:08:45.640 --> 00:08:47.310
But you’re fine, right?

00:08:47.310 --> 00:08:51.300
It’s a very popular bridge, driven by thousands
of people every day and night.

00:08:51.300 --> 00:08:55.691
It just so happens to be completely empty
at an ordinary time of night, and that you

00:08:55.691 --> 00:09:00.760
can see the dark outline of a figure in the
distance, standing in the middle of the road.

00:09:00.760 --> 00:09:06.110
As you drive closer and closer, you start
to make out the figure a bit more.

00:09:06.110 --> 00:09:13.840
A circular head, a tall, wide body, and two
more circles on top of that round, ball head.

00:09:13.840 --> 00:09:20.030
Closer, a little closer, and… wait, is that-
There’s absolutely no way that’s who you

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:21.210
think it is.

00:09:21.210 --> 00:09:24.090
Is that a Mickey Mouse costume standing in
the middle of the road?

00:09:24.090 --> 00:09:28.230
It apparently is, and it seems like it’s
not getting out of the way.

00:09:28.230 --> 00:09:33.010
You honk your horn, but the overgrown rat
doesn’t listen, it’s still standing there,

00:09:33.010 --> 00:09:34.010
unmoving.

00:09:34.010 --> 00:09:35.010
You slow down.

00:09:35.010 --> 00:09:38.901
You know what Disney’s legal team is capable
of and you are absolutely not going to go

00:09:38.901 --> 00:09:43.070
to jail for running over Mickey Mouse, so
if he’s not moving out of the way, you will

00:09:43.070 --> 00:09:44.190
instead.

00:09:44.190 --> 00:09:48.630
You try to maneuver around the stationary
mascot, but suddenly, out of nowhere, the

00:09:48.630 --> 00:09:52.260
thing leaps fifteen feet into the air and
jumps onto your hood.

00:09:52.260 --> 00:09:56.980
You scream as the Mickey mascot scitters across
the roof of your car, clawing and tearing

00:09:56.980 --> 00:09:58.790
at the sunroof, trying to get in.

00:09:58.790 --> 00:10:02.070
You push your foot on the gas as hard as you
can, with enough force to propel Mickey from

00:10:02.070 --> 00:10:04.170
the roof, but it’s not enough.

00:10:04.170 --> 00:10:08.190
The mascot hits the ground, but immediately
gets back up and starts running after your

00:10:08.190 --> 00:10:09.260
car.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:13.810
Almost instantaneously, it catches up to your
car again, and uses its strength to pry off

00:10:13.810 --> 00:10:18.070
the door on the driver’s side of the car,
exposing you and causing you to lose control

00:10:18.070 --> 00:10:19.070
of your vehicle.

00:10:19.070 --> 00:10:24.560
You swerve, crashing into the side of the
bridge and banging your head off of the steering

00:10:24.560 --> 00:10:25.560
wheel.

00:10:25.560 --> 00:10:29.290
You never thought your life would result in
death by Mickey Mouse, but the rapidly approaching

00:10:29.290 --> 00:10:31.660
costumed creature seems to be saying otherwise.

00:10:31.660 --> 00:10:37.600
The Mickey creature bends down, and uses both
of its gloved hands to grab you from your

00:10:37.600 --> 00:10:42.530
car seat with enough force to break the seatbelt
and give you minor whiplash from being flung

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:44.260
into the air so quickly.

00:10:44.260 --> 00:10:49.200
This is it, you know it’s over, and you
don’t even know what’s going on or why

00:10:49.200 --> 00:10:50.290
this is happening.

00:10:50.290 --> 00:10:54.320
You’re just another victim of something
you don’t understand, like the countless

00:10:54.320 --> 00:10:56.690
dead you spent your life researching.

00:10:56.690 --> 00:10:58.330
Or so you think.

00:10:58.330 --> 00:11:02.490
Just when you assume that it’s all over,
a shot rings out from across the bridge, and

00:11:02.490 --> 00:11:07.190
you see a salvo of bullets pepper Mickey Mouse’s
back, carefully missing you with impressively

00:11:07.190 --> 00:11:08.580
accurate precision.

00:11:08.580 --> 00:11:12.860
Mickey drops you, banging your head on the
concrete, and runs towards where the bullets

00:11:12.860 --> 00:11:14.290
are coming from.

00:11:14.290 --> 00:11:17.740
Several armored, heavily armed soldiers appear
from the side of the bridge and circle the

00:11:17.740 --> 00:11:18.740
mouse.

00:11:18.740 --> 00:11:21.850
They fire again, but it has little effect
on the mascot.

00:11:21.850 --> 00:11:25.330
Once again, he lunges forward, knocking a
soldier off his feet.

00:11:25.330 --> 00:11:29.120
The mascot dashes off into the distance, leaping
over the side of the bridge.

00:11:29.120 --> 00:11:34.290
Though no splash is heard in the water below,
you don’t see the mascot landing or even

00:11:34.290 --> 00:11:35.290
escaping.

00:11:35.290 --> 00:11:38.010
It’s like he was never there in the first
place.

00:11:38.010 --> 00:11:42.920
But at least it’s gone now, and you have
these unknown soldiers to thank for your,

00:11:42.920 --> 00:11:45.140
wait, is that an SCP Foundation logo?

00:11:45.140 --> 00:11:48.000
Oh no, they’re Foundation Task Force operatives.

00:11:48.000 --> 00:11:51.180
Before you’re able to fully regain your
senses, you can already hear the Task Force

00:11:51.180 --> 00:11:54.980
captain telling his underling to prep you
for amnestics and an interview.

00:11:54.980 --> 00:11:59.420
The soldier approaches you, and you’re thankfully
able to muster out a few choice words.

00:11:59.420 --> 00:12:01.610
Namely, “Wait, wait, wait, wait, wait!

00:12:01.610 --> 00:12:02.610
I’m with you guys!

00:12:02.610 --> 00:12:03.780
I’m a junior researcher!”

00:12:03.780 --> 00:12:06.020
The captain pauses and laughs to himself.

00:12:06.020 --> 00:12:08.440
What are the odds?

00:12:08.440 --> 00:12:11.990
After you’re processed and taken to the
nearest facility, where your identity as a

00:12:11.990 --> 00:12:16.730
card carrying member of the SCP Foundation
is confirmed, you’re let in on what exactly

00:12:16.730 --> 00:12:18.990
it was that you just saw back there.

00:12:18.990 --> 00:12:25.230
As it turns out, you had an encounter with
SCP-3640, an anomaly centering around a set

00:12:25.230 --> 00:12:30.790
of travel brochures that advertise self-guided
tours of all of Florida’s paranormal hotspots.

00:12:30.790 --> 00:12:36.020
If someone reads the brochure and goes to
a location at a set time, just like you did,

00:12:36.020 --> 00:12:41.750
they’ll be preyed upon by a mysterious,
predatory entity or set of entities that resemble

00:12:41.750 --> 00:12:46.270
costumed mascot characters owned by the Walt
Disney Company.

00:12:46.270 --> 00:12:51.540
Mickey, Donald, Goofy, the task force captain
explains that they’re all there, and they’re

00:12:51.540 --> 00:12:53.680
all over the state of Florida.

00:12:53.680 --> 00:12:55.540
Hundreds of mascots, maybe more.

00:12:55.540 --> 00:13:00.700
They’re fast, dangerous, and the Foundation
knows remarkably little about them.

00:13:00.700 --> 00:13:06.000
Including how they grow, reproduce, or even
consume their prey.

00:13:06.000 --> 00:13:09.820
All of the known hotspots advertised in the
pamphlet are routinely watched by members

00:13:09.820 --> 00:13:15.840
of the Pest Control mobile task force, where
operatives are authorized to neutralize SCP-3640

00:13:15.840 --> 00:13:17.460
entities with lethal force.

00:13:17.460 --> 00:13:22.460
Which is how that Task Force was able to thankfully
show up at the right moment and save your

00:13:22.460 --> 00:13:23.720
life.

00:13:23.720 --> 00:13:29.570
SCP-3640 only attack those who read the brochures,
and haven’t been seen being hostile or hunting

00:13:29.570 --> 00:13:32.480
outside of the areas specified by the pamphlet.

00:13:32.480 --> 00:13:38.450
After you recollect yourself and thank them,
the captain hands you a file briefing on SCP-3640,

00:13:38.450 --> 00:13:42.620
gives you a stern warning, and tells you to
familiarize yourself with it before you leave

00:13:42.620 --> 00:13:43.870
the facility.

00:13:43.870 --> 00:13:46.490
What a way to start your vacation, you think.

00:13:46.490 --> 00:13:50.640
Just when you thought you were able to escape
the daily horrors of working for the Foundation,

00:13:50.640 --> 00:13:53.200
you stumble onto an anomaly yourself.

00:13:53.200 --> 00:13:57.740
But you undoubtedly have more questions about
SCP-3640.

00:13:57.740 --> 00:14:02.000
After all, anyone would after witnessing as
weird and strange an anomaly as that in the

00:14:02.000 --> 00:14:03.000
wild.

00:14:03.000 --> 00:14:07.910
You ask the captain why the Foundation hasn’t
captured an SCP-3640 instance, especially

00:14:07.910 --> 00:14:10.060
if they’re so common in the Florida area.

00:14:10.060 --> 00:14:14.820
He sits down, sighs, and explains that the
Foundation did try, awhile back.

00:14:14.820 --> 00:14:20.910
It was a standard D-Class test, held in the
St. Johns River, the location of a supposed

00:14:20.910 --> 00:14:22.090
“river monster”.

00:14:22.090 --> 00:14:25.960
The D-Class personnel was dropped off at the
river bank and told to follow the instructions

00:14:25.960 --> 00:14:27.180
in the pamphlet.

00:14:27.180 --> 00:14:31.570
If they spotted a mascot, they were to shoot
at it with a tranquilizer gun.

00:14:31.570 --> 00:14:35.260
After dredging through the river for a few
minutes and being distracted by a neat looking

00:14:35.260 --> 00:14:41.820
alligator, the D-Class eventually came head
to head with none other than Donald Duck himself,

00:14:41.820 --> 00:14:46.010
who emerged from the river and immediately
began moving towards the D-Class.

00:14:46.010 --> 00:14:50.470
The D-Class naturally freaked out completely,
and ran away from the scene, but Donald was

00:14:50.470 --> 00:14:52.520
simply too fast.

00:14:52.520 --> 00:14:56.730
Just when he thought he was safe, the Donald
mascot emerged from the shadows and knocked

00:14:56.730 --> 00:14:58.970
the camera and radio off of the D-Class’s
head.

00:14:58.970 --> 00:15:03.900
There were sounds of a struggle, but the D-Class
never established contact again.

00:15:03.900 --> 00:15:08.250
However, his subdermal tracking transmitters
continued to operate, and before they went

00:15:08.250 --> 00:15:13.360
offline completely, they luckily detected
the location of the D-Class’s body.

00:15:13.360 --> 00:15:16.990
It was just outside of the EPCOT amusement
park.

00:15:16.990 --> 00:15:20.110
Engaged by the captain’s story, you ask
him what happened next.

00:15:20.110 --> 00:15:23.870
Surely, the Foundation launched an assault
on EPCOT to figure out what happened to the

00:15:23.870 --> 00:15:25.030
D-Class, right?

00:15:25.030 --> 00:15:28.220
The captain grunts, and tells you that the
rest is classified.

00:15:28.220 --> 00:15:29.860
But you’re not satisfied.

00:15:29.860 --> 00:15:33.920
You’re refusing to move until you figure
out what happened to this D-Class.

00:15:33.920 --> 00:15:39.540
The captain rolls his eyes, and perhaps feeling
sorry for you, decides to tell you the rest

00:15:39.540 --> 00:15:40.540
of the story.

00:15:40.540 --> 00:15:45.860
Him and his team were deployed just outside
of the EPCOT theme park, right next to a one

00:15:45.860 --> 00:15:49.480
story, concrete hut, where the D-Class’s
location was tracked.

00:15:49.480 --> 00:15:53.580
They were equipped with heavy arms, a net
launcher, and a flamethrower, all perfect

00:15:53.580 --> 00:15:56.410
weapons for subduing these deadly mascots.

00:15:56.410 --> 00:16:00.850
While Lambda-12 was typically used to hunting
anomalous bugs and pests, they figured that

00:16:00.850 --> 00:16:05.350
hunting down Donald Duck and Minnie Mouse
was more or less the same thing, when you

00:16:05.350 --> 00:16:08.060
squint really hard and pretend that they have
wings.

00:16:08.060 --> 00:16:12.160
The task force broke into the hut, revealing
it to be a maintenance shed with a mysterious

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:14.921
trap door in the middle of the floor.

00:16:14.921 --> 00:16:18.850
Underneath, a ladder led to a tunnel system,
similar to the ones built underneath the Disney

00:16:18.850 --> 00:16:22.420
Parks that the employees use to get around
from park to park.

00:16:22.420 --> 00:16:27.710
The team spotted several dressing rooms and
storage rooms, all empty and devoid of any

00:16:27.710 --> 00:16:28.710
life.

00:16:28.710 --> 00:16:32.940
After some exploration, the team followed
a low rumbling noise to a closed door.

00:16:32.940 --> 00:16:38.780
They slowly opened it, revealing an abandoned
boiler room, with a white mascot costume at

00:16:38.780 --> 00:16:43.030
the foot of the boiler, curled up around an
unknown object.

00:16:43.030 --> 00:16:47.540
An operative approached the costume and poked
it with her rifle, identifying it as an empty

00:16:47.540 --> 00:16:49.360
Daisy Duck costume.

00:16:49.360 --> 00:16:54.790
The team examined it further, and found a
human arm bone inside the suit.

00:16:54.790 --> 00:16:58.380
Disgusting, to be sure, but nothing the task
force hadn’t seen before.

00:16:58.380 --> 00:17:02.310
They turned over the suit to examine the object
it was curled around, discovering it to be

00:17:02.310 --> 00:17:06.139
a purple, plastic egg, with an embryo inside.

00:17:06.139 --> 00:17:08.890
Scattered across the floor were more eggshells.

00:17:08.890 --> 00:17:13.049
The squad gathered them, as well as the bones
of the D-Class in the costume, to bring back

00:17:13.049 --> 00:17:14.100
to the facility.

00:17:14.100 --> 00:17:19.100
Suddenly, the task force heard noises in the
distance, and assumed an attack formation.

00:17:19.100 --> 00:17:23.709
They noticed the floor of the entrance they
came in was now covered in dark fluid and

00:17:23.709 --> 00:17:25.319
polyester stuffing.

00:17:25.319 --> 00:17:29.809
The trail of liquid exactly matched their
path of infiltration into the tunnel.

00:17:29.809 --> 00:17:33.840
After determining the situation to be safe,
the squad carefully left the tunnel the way

00:17:33.840 --> 00:17:37.860
they came, bringing the costume and the egg
with them.

00:17:37.860 --> 00:17:42.860
After several weeks, the egg hatched into
a miniature stuffed donald duck toy.

00:17:42.860 --> 00:17:47.990
The Foundation dissected it, discovering it
to contain a plastic endoskeleton and a rudimentary

00:17:47.990 --> 00:17:50.610
polyester stuffing muscular system inside.

00:17:50.610 --> 00:17:53.789
And that was everything the captain had to
say.

00:17:53.789 --> 00:18:00.000
There was never any other leads on the SCP-3640
anomaly, just strangeness and inexplicable

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:03.510
inability to capture or understand the mascots.

00:18:03.510 --> 00:18:07.980
You thanked the captain for not only saving
you, but explaining what was going on.

00:18:07.980 --> 00:18:12.160
Before you left the facility to go back to
your regular, foundation-less vacation, you

00:18:12.160 --> 00:18:15.509
took another glance at the document the Captain
handed to you.

00:18:15.509 --> 00:18:21.190
On the back page was a chilling letter, dated
from 1979, written to Florida governor Reuben

00:18:21.190 --> 00:18:23.700
Askew by the Walt Disney Company.

00:18:23.700 --> 00:18:25.379
It read:

00:18:25.379 --> 00:18:30.649
The Walt Disney Company thanks you for your
cooperation in this matter regarding the unlicensed

00:18:30.649 --> 00:18:33.070
Walt Disney character operators.

00:18:33.070 --> 00:18:37.299
Please pass along the following information,
collected by the outstanding men and women

00:18:37.299 --> 00:18:41.679
of the City of Orlando's Police Department,
to the Florida National Guard:

00:18:41.679 --> 00:18:46.860
If a character is spotted, call to get its
attention and then rapidly flash your flashlights

00:18:46.860 --> 00:18:48.130
at the costume.

00:18:48.130 --> 00:18:51.029
If it does not flinch, fire on sight.

00:18:51.029 --> 00:18:55.340
Aim at the head if possible; else, aim at
the knees to disable them and then finish

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:57.110
them off with head shots.

00:18:57.110 --> 00:19:00.080
Body shots have been shown to lack effectiveness.

00:19:00.080 --> 00:19:02.830
Deceased characters are to be incinerated.

00:19:02.830 --> 00:19:05.360
No other means of disposal are advised.

00:19:05.360 --> 00:19:10.330
We are currently pursuing alternative legal
means of shutting down these unlicensed operators

00:19:10.330 --> 00:19:13.509
and hope to achieve a settlement within the
end of the year.

00:19:13.509 --> 00:19:16.500
Cordially yours,
The Walt Disney Company

00:19:16.500 --> 00:19:22.871
Now go watch “SCP-2805 - Disney on Ice”
and “SCP-823 - Carnival of Horrors” for

00:19:22.871 --> 00:19:25.679
more anomalous theme park madness from SCP
Explained!

